 "suggested_experiment_name": "AGN_Spins_2020",
 "coupling_convention": "1/f_a [GeV^-1]",
 "notes": "Exclusion limit on axion decay constant from AGN black hole spin measurements via superradiance (arXiv:2012.12790, Figure 6). The paper derives bounds by noting that if ultralight scalar particles existed and coupled to black holes, they would trigger superradiance - extracting rotational energy and causing the black hole to spin down. Since the observed AGN spins remain high, superradiance must be either absent (weak coupling scenario shown here) or self-suppressed by strong self-interactions. The figure shows multiple colored regions corresponding to different AGN measurements from Table 2 (M87, Mrk 110, NGC 4151, Ark 120, 1H0707-495, IRAS13224-3809, MRK 335, 1H0419-577). White region below the curves is ruled out. The boundary represents the combined constraint from all measured AGNs. Extracted via image analysis and converted from f_axion [GeV] to canonical variable 1/f_a [GeV^-1]. Mass range: 2.9\u00d710^-21 to 1.7\u00d710^-17 eV as stated in paper summary.",
